[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Framework mutation physical process paths

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VERIFY-FRAMEWORK-PATH-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Short physical managed mutation paths
STATEMENT: >>>
The framework mutation supervisor shall construct isolated managed source, build and report paths beneath an existing physical artifact root, resolving intermediate directory junctions or symbolic links. On Windows it shall reject a root whose projected transport fixture executable path reaches 240 characters before creating a campaign directory. It shall retain the logical source identity, physical work root and copied source/input hashes separately from the source-scoped worker locks.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/FrameworkMutations.cs; scripts/Run-VerifiedSoak.ps1.
Verification: tests/FrameworkPhysicalPaths.Tests.ps1 and scripts/tests/SoakSupervision.Tests.ps1. Evidence: evidence/framework-physical-paths.json and docs/framework-physical-paths.md.
The Windows guard is a conservative process-path policy, not a claim that every executable or tool accepts all shorter paths. Linux has no arbitrary Windows length limit. The approved native fixture smoke input does not qualify a new source-pinned overnight campaign.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REF-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VERIFY-FRAMEWORK-PATH-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Actual transport fixture launch preflight
STATEMENT: >>>
Before Stryker baseline execution the supervisor shall build the copied managed test project and launch its actual transport fixture apphost, close its input and verify its output and exit status within one shared deadline bounded by ten seconds and the remaining campaign time. Expired budgets shall prevent dispatch. Input, exit and inherited-output drainage shall share that deadline; owned-process cleanup shall have a separate two-second allowance that cannot authorize further work. A build or launch failure shall fail the framework report instead of entering mutation execution.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/FrameworkMutations.cs, PreflightFixture and managed-preflight-build.log.
Verification: tests/FrameworkPhysicalPaths.Tests.ps1 exercises the same actual executable through an overlong logical junction alias and the resolved physical directory, plus missing-fixture failure propagation. The launcher regression verifies explicit physical-root propagation into the owned worker and its manifest.
Deadline regressions: tests/FrameworkDeadlines.Tests.ps1 and its owned FrameworkDeadlineFixture exercise zero-budget refusal, a delayed child, inherited output after parent exit, owned-child reaping and expired campaign tool dispatch. Follow-up evidence: evidence/framework-deadline-followup.json. Original path-fix logs and historical coverage scope are identified in evidence/framework-physical-paths.json. A bounded mutation sample is separate from complete framework or release qualification.
<<<
